{
  "title": "Projectile Target Challenge: Pick Angle and Speed",
  "description": "A launcher sits at the left end of a flat 70 m field with marks every 10 m. A red target pad with a flag sits down the field. Set the launch angle and speed, then press Launch. The ball flies along its arc and leaves a trail. When it lands, readouts show the landing distance, how far it missed and on which side, the flight time and the highest point. Hit targets at 30 m, 45 m and 18 m using no more than 10 launches.",
  "experience": "game",
  "behavior": "rules",
  "controlProfile": "inspect",
  "stepped": true,
  "game": {
    "objective": "Hit 3 targets (at 30 m, 45 m, then 18 m) with no more than 10 launches. A hit lands within 1.5 m of the target's centre, edges included.",
    "hint": "At the same speed, angles that add up to 90° (like 30° and 60°) land at the same distance, and 45° goes farthest. Doubling the speed makes the shot go four times as far."
  },
