  "assumptions": [
    "This is a simplified simulation: no air resistance, and the ball starts at ground level on flat ground.",
    "Gravity is 9.8 m/s² straight down. Sideways speed stays constant; only the vertical speed changes.",
    "Each point of the flight is computed exactly from the projectile formulas, so landing distance = speed² × sin(2 × angle) ÷ 9.8.",
    "The ball is treated as a point; it is drawn as a 1 m ball, raised by its radius so it sits on the ground. The red pad has the 1.5 m hit radius.",
    "Every flight plays over 2 seconds on screen, so the on-screen time does not match the flight-time readout. While flying, your previous arc shows as a faded line (solid, not dashed).",
    "Targets come in a fixed order (30 m, 45 m, 18 m); Reset starts the same challenge again and clears the score and trails. Real balls land shorter because of air drag."
  ],
